        "original_id": "6aa9eec3-de7b-5eed-8ecd-9f31700c35e7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Bilerman, Vic Chesnutt, Basia Bulat\n- Organizations: Arcade Fire, Thee Silver Mt. Zion Memorial Orchestra & Tra-La-La Band\n- Products: Funeral, Oh, My Darling\n- Places: Montreal, Athens, Georgia\n- Topics: music recording, production, drumming\n\nFacts:\n- James Victor Chesnutt was born on November 12, 1964, and he was an American singer-songwriter from Athens, Georgia.\n- Howard Bilerman was a former member of Arcade Fire, and he recorded and played drums on the band's debut album Funeral.\n- Howard Bilerman also recorded on releases by Thee Silver Mt. Zion Memorial Orchestra & Tra-La-La Band, Vic Chesnutt, Basia Bulat, Peter Peter, Rich Aucoin, and Angela Desveaux.\n- Basia Bulat met Howard Bilerman in 2006 and asked him to work with her.\n- Oh, My Darling was recorded in Montreal and was produced by Howard Bilerman.\n- James Victor Chesnutt died on December 25, 2009.",
